        "text": "But there are some risks to centralized exchanges. They can be hacked or the operating entity could face financial difficulties. In both cases, user funds might be at risk. On the other hand, decentralized exchanges operate very differently. There are no custodians involved in decentralized exchanges. In fact, we can refer to decentralized exchanges as non custodial exchanges. They cut out the middleman and operate in a trustless environment. You can also think of them as peer to peer exchanges, where transactions are done between users directly and entirely based on smart contracts, which are self executing computer programs on a blockchain that run when predetermined conditions are met. Here's what happens when you trade on a decentralized exchange. Instead of depositing your funds to the exchange's wallet, you're trading directly from your own wallet. When a trade is executed, the transaction is completed directly on the blockchain using smart contracts.",
